      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The plasma concentrations of five proteinase inhibitors (alpha 2-plasmin inhibitor, alpha 2-antitrypsin, antithrombin III, C1-inactivator, alpha 2-macroglobulin) in healthy school-age children were determined by electroimmunoassay. The concentrations of the same proteins were further determined in children with a familial risk of developing ischaemic heart disease. A significantly lower concentration of antithrombin III and a higher concentration of fibrinogen was found in this group."},
